When you compile nethack, I would suggest putting in a -DMSDOS in the
command line, just in case it doesn't get defined when it should be.

In config.h, in the "FUN STUFF" area, undefine everything but
REDO, HARD, WIZARD, and EXPLORE_MODE.

Also, in the makefile, for Turbo C 2.0, change the -Z in the CFLAGS=
definition to -Z- (according to the makefile).

Termcap.lib is as far as I can tell, necessary.  

Do not change PCCONF.H (I didn't).

Use NDmake4.5 to make it.

Versions:
NDmake4.5
Turbo C 2.0
Microsoft Link 3.05
Turbo tlink 2.0 (For the smaller files)

Also, READ INSTALL.DOS!!!

I've gotten it to work, so take heart, you can, too.
When I say "work", I mean start up, ask me "who are you?", and the various
character class questions ("Do you want to be a ....."). Then it draws out the
first room of the first level, and then says "At gets null at 0 0",
"Program in disorder, perhaps you'd better quit!"  I'm not sure yet, why.

This is Nethack with update1 installed...
MSDOS3.3

